KZ3 patch 1065 (SPU pass 48, finding network pass 15): the SPU DMA repeat guard (runtime/spu/spu_dma.h) halted an SPU
after 256 consecutive identical transfers, counted in process-wide statics. A job polling a main-memory word with GET
until another SPU or the PPU changes it issues exactly that, so in KZ3's level 2 wid 7's job (LS pc 0x1CEAC / 0x1CA50)
was halted mid-poll, its lane never returned ([pm-end] halted=1, [spurs-stuck] wid=7) and the game froze (339 s and
538 s into the level, 2 of 2; with the limit out of reach 2 of 2 played 670 s). Now: the counter lives in the context's
mfc_engine (per lane), the halt is off unless SPU_DMA_REPEAT_LIMIT=N is set, and a long repeat is logged once per
(image, pc) site after SPU_DMA_REPEAT_LOG transfers (default 4096, 0 = never) as a diagnostic that leaves the SPU alone.
Host test: tools/spu/test_spu_dma_repeat.sh. Upstream candidate (general).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.17.0 (SPU pass 95): kept over #383 (process-wide wall-time halt, 1 ms back-off): KZ3's default never reaches the limit.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): ours over upstream's per-thread repeat watchdog with yield/back-off (same env name SPU_DMA_REPEAT_LOG, different meaning upstream).

